# Proposal

Measure and compare the vocabulary distributions and high-frequency words across two separate works by the same author.

Compare the word frequency distributions of those works against a work by a different author to identify unique vocabulary signatures.

**Primary Author:** F. Colburn Adams

**Book 1:** *Manuel Pereira; Or, The Sovereign Rule of South Carolina*

https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/4680/pg4680.txt

**Book 2:** *Our World; Or, the Slaveholder's Daughter*

https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/4677/pg4677.txt

**Secondary Author:** Robert Louis Stevenson

**Book 1:** *Treasure Island*

https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/120/pg120.txt

I plan to use the NLTK and BeautifulSoup libraries to ingest, clean, process, and analyze the text data.

I will compare the vocabulary distributions and high-frequency words between the two works by F. Colburn Adams. I will then compare these results with *Treasure Island* by Robert Louis Stevenson to identify differences and similarities in vocabulary usage.

I will use Matplotlib to visualize the results using graphs such as word-frequency charts and vocabulary distribution comparisons.
